`opentelemetry-api`: implement the declarative configuration Instrumentation Configuration API in `opentelemetry._configuration`, so an instrumentation library can read its own configuration without depending on the SDK. `ConfigProperties` is a typed read view over a configuration node, with `get_string`/`get_bool`/`get_int`/`get_float`, `get_config`/`get_config_list`, the sequence getters `get_string_list`/`get_bool_list`/`get_int_list`/`get_float_list`, and `keys`. `get_config_provider`/`set_config_provider` hold the global `ConfigProvider`, following the set-once, proxy-default semantics of `get_tracer_provider`/`set_tracer_provider`. In `opentelemetry-configuration`, `configure_sdk` installs that provider, built from the `instrumentation/development` node as the configuration file wrote it.
